  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Rewrite each sum in sigma notation, starting each sum at $n=1$. Do not evaluate it.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p12-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$1^3+2^3+3^3+\\cdots+40^3$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{40}n^3$",
          "worked": "The $n$th term is $n^3$, and the final term has $n=40$.\n$$\\sum_{n=1}^{40}n^3$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$1+\\frac12+\\frac13+\\cdots+\\frac1{40}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{40}\\left(\\frac1n\\right)$",
          "worked": "The $n$th term is $\\frac1n$, and the final denominator is $40$.\n$$\\sum_{n=1}^{40}\\left(\\frac1n\\right)$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$3+4+5+\\cdots+22$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{20}(n+2)$",
          "worked": "Starting at $n=1$, the term rule is $n+2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}n+2&=22\\\\n&=20\\end{align*}$$\nHence the sum is $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{20}(n+2)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$2+2^2+2^3+\\cdots+2^{12}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{12}2^n$",
          "worked": "The first term is $2^1$, so the term rule is $2^n$. The final exponent is $12$.\n$$\\sum_{n=1}^{12}2^n$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$-1+2-3+\\cdots+10$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{10}(-1)^n n$",
          "worked": "The magnitudes are $n$. The factor $(-1)^n$ is negative for odd $n$ and positive for even $n$, giving the required signs. The last term has $n=10$.\n$$\\sum_{n=1}^{10}(-1)^n n$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$1-2+3-\\cdots-10$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{10}(-1)^{n+1}n$ or $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{10}(-1)^{n-1}n$",
          "worked": "The magnitudes are $n$. The factor $(-1)^{n+1}$ is positive for odd $n$ and negative for even $n$. The last term has $n=10$.\n$$\\sum_{n=1}^{10}(-1)^{n+1}n$$\nSince $n+1$ and $n-1$ differ by $2$, an equivalent form is $\\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{10}(-1)^{n-1}n$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
